{{Term/Store|Hateno Cow|Hateno Cows|Series, BotW, TotK|plural}} are recurring [[Creature]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref>{{Cite|'''Hateno Cow'''|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|'''Hateno Cow'''|Hyrule Compendium|TotK}}</ref>

==Characteristics==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|Hateno Cow}}
Hateno Cows are domesticated versions of [[Water Buffalo]] that can be found grazing at settlements in [[East Necluda]] and the [[Faron Grasslands]].<ref>{{Cite|These wild cows come equipped with big, strong horns. They live off grass that grows near the waterfront. Their meat is considered to be high quality, so they're a common target among hunters. Fun fact: the domesticated Hateno cow, often raised in villages, was bred through selective breeding using these.|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref> They originate at [[Hateno Pasture]] in [[Hateno Village]], and they are kept as livestock for their [[Fresh Milk]].<ref name="Compendium">{{Cite|Originating in Hateno Village, these cows are kept as livestock primarily for their milk. Their horns are smaller than a water buffalo's, and they're much more docile and therefore easier to raise. Their horns are decorated with bright colors when taken out to pasture.|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref> When they are out to pasture, their horns are decorated with bright colors.<ref name="Compendium"/> It is impossible for [[Link]] to damage or kill Hateno Cows, and as a result, they offer no drops.

